+"""The names of ROOT's own classes, as ROOT 6.40's headers declare them.
+
+A file describes every class it holds, and ``TClass::Init`` warns of one nothing has a
+dictionary for - but only of a class the program's own: a file describing ROOT's ``TGeoAtt``
+or ``TBasket`` opens in silence, because ROOT's libraries were built with those dictionaries.
+Nothing here can ask ROOT which classes those are, and a name's spelling tells nothing - a
+program's class is called ``TEmcl`` or ``TCedarEvent`` as readily as ROOT's is called
+``TRegexp`` - so they are listed.
+
+Every class a ROOT 6.40.04 header declares with a ``ClassDef`` is here, as
+
+    python - <<'PY'
+    import re, pathlib
+    pattern = re.compile(r"^\\s*ClassDef[A-Za-z]*\\(\\s*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z_0-9]*)", re.M)
+    names = {found for path in pathlib.Path(include).glob("*.h")
+             for found in pattern.findall(path.read_text(errors="ignore"))}
+    PY
+
+gives them for ``include`` the ``include`` directory of the ``root`` 6.40.04 conda-forge
+build, 1632 of them. Only the headers at its top are read: the classes of a subdirectory's
+library - ``TMVA/Event``, whose name a roottest program's own ``Event`` shares - are the ones
+ROOT does not have loaded when it opens a file, and ROOT names a program's class of that name.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+__all__ = ["ROOT_CLASSES"]
+
